{
 "fps": 30,
 "frames": 1460,
 "dur": 48.656,
 "target": 45.0,
 "lines": [
  {
   "text": "Lola crossed the high wire with a toothpick, wobbling like a noodle.",
   "s": 0.12,
   "e": 3.172
  },
  {
   "text": "Ringmaster Barty had shrunk her pole. \"The customer is always right!\" So why do tightrope walkers carry long poles?",
   "s": 3.372,
   "e": 9.117
  },
  {
   "text": "Complaint one: \"Her pole knocked off my hat.\" So Barty sawed it in half.",
   "s": 9.417,
   "e": 12.852
  },
  {
   "text": "Peanut the elephant gasped. He's been practicing on a garden hose for years.",
   "s": 13.052,
   "e": 16.412
  },
  {
   "text": "Complaint two: \"Now it blocks my popcorn.\" Barty handed her a toothpick. \"The customer is always right!\"",
   "s": 16.612,
   "e": 21.805
  },
  {
   "text": "Lola swayed left, right, then spun around the wire like a rotisserie chicken.",
   "s": 21.925,
   "e": 25.35
  },
  {
   "text": "Complaint three: \"Watching her made me seasick.\"",
   "s": 25.55,
   "e": 27.395
  },
  {
   "text": "So what was the pole doing?",
   "s": 27.515,
   "e": 28.538
  },
  {
   "text": "A long pole is hard to turn, like spinning on an office chair holding a ladder.",
   "s": 28.838,
   "e": 32.377
  },
  {
   "text": "So when Lola tips, she tips slowly, with time to fix it.",
   "s": 32.777,
   "e": 35.313
  },
  {
   "text": "A toothpick tips you over like a dropped pencil.",
   "s": 35.513,
   "e": 37.582
  },
  {
   "text": "Barty brought the long pole back. Lola strolled across, eating popcorn.",
   "s": 37.782,
   "e": 41.313
  },
  {
   "text": "Peanut got a pole too. He's still on the garden hose.",
   "s": 41.513,
   "e": 43.897
  },
  {
   "text": "Barty's new sign: \"The customer is always right. Except about poles.\"",
   "s": 44.097,
   "e": 47.356
  }
 ],
